  "scope": "Existing signature decomposition receives explicit per-region effects and a trace label, independent of a declaration ID. Original API delegates with its original effect lookup. Native test decomposes the actual stored callback signature with its real generics and instantiated lifetime: forward Context, Result Context output/backward state, forward failure and forward/backward divergence retained. Backward cannot-fail follows existing decomposition contract; not a proof of arbitrary callback behavior. No new dynamic AST/Pure application or type-field translation.",
  "validation": "Isolated build and forced Charon ML tests passed. Native tests preserve actual signature and reject six unsupported signatures; all six actual transparent regular signatures produce equal decompositions using old API and explicit helper within candidate. This API equality is not an independent unpatched-binary comparison or semantic preservation proof. Fresh-source gate additionally checks nine LLBC modifications, actual six-body borrow-check success, strict Lean rejection and no output.",
  "remaining": "Full callback value/application in symbolic AST and Pure; actual higher-ranked function pointer field type translation with borrow/effect closure; heap and host write-back correctness; unknown callee implementation semantics and dispatch table; tool correctness/source/compiler/LLVM/Wasm/IC/ledger correspondence. Candidate remains unadopted; no Rust all-input or whole-program theorem."
